# Naming

Consistent names reduce cognitive load across repos and AI-assisted edits.

## Files and folders

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| React component | `PascalCase.tsx` | `PosTicket.tsx` |
| Page | `PascalCase.tsx` | `Catalogo.tsx`, `POS.tsx` |
| Hook | `use*.ts` | `usePosCart.ts` |
| POS/shop UI | `components/pos/` or `pages/` | `PosTicket.tsx` — no `features/` folders |
| API route module | `*_routes.py` | `pos_routes.py` |
| Helper next to routes | `snake_case.py` | `shop_fulfillment.py` |
| Test | colocated `*.test.ts` / `backend/tests/test_*.py` | `phoneInput.test.ts` |
| SQL migration | `NNNNNN_snake_description.sql` | `000001_app_schema.sql` |

## TypeScript / JavaScript symbols

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Variables, functions | `camelCase` | `createSale`, `lineCount` |
| Types, interfaces, enums | `PascalCase` | `SaleRecord`, `PaymentMethod` |
| Constants (true const) | `SCREAMING_SNAKE` or `camelCase` for grouped const objects | `VENTA_LIBRE_PRODUCT_ID` |
| React component | `PascalCase` | `function PosHeader()` |
| Context | `*Provider`, `use*` hook | `AuthProvider`, `useAuth` |
| Boolean vars | prefix `is`, `has`, `can` | `isSupabaseConfigured`, `canAccessPos` |

## Python symbols

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Modules | `snake_case` | `pos_routes.py` |
| Functions, variables | `snake_case` | `require_pos_staff` |
| Classes | `PascalCase` | `PosSaleCreate` |
| Private helpers | `_leading_underscore` | `_fetch_sale_by_id` |
| Pydantic fields (internal) | `snake_case` with camelCase **alias** for JSON | `product_id` / `productId` |

## Database (Postgres)

| Kind | Convention | Example |
|------|------------|---------|
| Schema | lowercase product name | `<app>` |
| Tables | `snake_case`, plural nouns | `pos_sales`, `catalog_products` |
| Columns | `snake_case` | `unit_price_pesos`, `staff_user_id` |
| RPC functions | `snake_case` verb phrase | `create_pos_sale` |
| RPC params | `p_snake_case` | `p_staff_user_id` |
| Indexes | `idx_<schema>_<table>_<cols>` | `idx_<app>_pos_sales_created_at` |

## JSON API (wire format)

- **camelCase** keys in request/response bodies: `productId`, `paymentMethod`, `createdAt`.
- Pydantic: `Field(alias="camelCase")` + `populate_by_name=True` on input models.
- Output models: declare fields directly in camelCase.

## URL paths

- lowercase, hyphen avoided — use slashes: `/api/pos/sales`, `/api/catalog/products`.
- Route params: `{saleId}` in OpenAPI docs; path `/api/pos/sales/{sale_id}` (FastAPI snake in path is OK if consistent).

## Environment variables

| Prefix | Where | Example |
|--------|-------|---------|
| `VITE_` | web build (public) | `VITE_BACKEND_URL`, `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` |
| none | API runtime (secret) | `SUPABASE_SERVICE_ROLE_KEY` |
| `R2_` | API storage | `R2_BUCKET_NAME` |
| `CORS_` | API optional | `CORS_EXTRA_ORIGINS` |

This repo wires **`VITE_BACKEND_URL`** only (`apiUrl.ts`, `vite-env.d.ts`). Do not rename to `VITE_API_URL` unless also changing code + Vercel env.

## Git branches and commits

- Branches: `feat/short-description`, `fix/short-description`, `chore/short-description`.
- Commits: imperative mood, ≤ 72 char subject — `fix(pos): validate deferred contact on pago_despues`.

## Product / domain terms (this vertical)

- Spanish UI labels; English in code identifiers is fine: `paymentMethod` value `pago_despues` not `payLater`.
- Roles: `admin`, `empleado` — lowercase string enums in DB and code.

## Anti-patterns

- ❌ `product_ts` when meaning product id — use `product_id`
- ❌ Mixed camelCase and snake_case in same JSON response
- ❌ `data`, `temp`, `handler1` — use domain names
- ❌ Spanish function names (`crearVenta`) — code in English, UI in Spanish
